<title>CROATIA: Croatian lending rate falls to 10.8 pct from 11.3.</title>
<headline>Croatian lending rate falls to 10.8 pct from 11.3.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Croatian average lending rate fell 50 basis points to 10.8 percent on Wednesday amid a slightly lower demand for kuna funds.</p>
<p>Settlements totalled 22.3 million against 60 million kuna offer. Most of the fresh borrowings were call money loans, granted at a steady rate of 10.5 percent.</p>
<p>Banks also rolled over old call money at 10.5 percent.</p>
<p>Insurers renewed one-week deals at 9.0 percent and three-week ones at 11 percent.</p>
<p>-- Sandra Kalogjera, Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
